# The policy set, owned by the repository owner (decision 0009 as amended
# 2026-09-16; #201 comments 5702359298 and 5702401684).
#
# GitHub reads this file for two things. Always: it auto-requests the owner's
# review on a pull request touching a path below, unless the owner authored it.
# Once `main-protect` carries its `pull_request` rule with
# `require_code_owner_review` (0009 step 6): such a pull request cannot merge
# without the owner's approving review on GitHub, which is then how the owner's
# approval of a policy change is given. Until that rule exists this file only
# requests reviews and enforces nothing, and the approval is given in session
# and recorded on #201.
#
# The owner is @tvofi and not the approver App: GitHub's docs list users and
# teams with explicit write access as code owners and name no App form. Every
# other path has no code owner; the App's approving review serves those.
# docs/HANDOVER.md is deliberately absent: it carries state, not rules.
#
# Nothing in the test gate opens this file (tests/closure.py lists it INERT).

/CLAUDE.md                                @tvofi
/AGENTS.md                                @tvofi
/.claude/rules/                           @tvofi
/.cursor/rules/                           @tvofi
/.claude/skills/steward/SKILL.md          @tvofi
/.claude/workflows/web-fragments.md       @tvofi
/tools/audit/briefs/                      @tvofi
# COMMON.md is the finder's contract and is not policy (CLAUDE.md says so);
# a later line with a path and no owner un-owns it, because the last matching
# pattern wins.
/tools/audit/briefs/COMMON.md
/tools/audit/README.md                    @tvofi
/tools/audit/harnesses/README.md          @tvofi
/tests/README.md                          @tvofi
/docs/decisions/                          @tvofi
/.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md         @tvofi
/.github/CODEOWNERS                       @tvofi
